{
    "background_story": "Aspen was a remarkable placoderm, a ancient armored fish that swam the Devonian seas. Her name, Aspen, was derived from the quaking aspen trees that lined the shores of the ancient lake where she lived. Aspen's body was covered in tough, bony plates that protected her from the predators of the time. But what set her apart was her unique ability to adapt to the changing environment. As the lake's waters fluctuated, Aspen's armor plates would shift and change color, allowing her to blend in seamlessly. Her remarkable camouflage skills made her a master of survival, and she thrived in the ancient ecosystem. Aspen's legacy lived on, as her descendants evolved into the modern fish that would eventually inhabit the world's oceans.",
